{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794252684,"nonce":"UvMCvuwf808a0rSPJtijnvNG0n4=","message":"Correction after measuring the fix: on macOS an allocated texture nothing draws into is not resident (an extra full-window texture per target left graphics memory unchanged), so skipping the unused MSAA texture saves nothing there. The real cost was the drawn resolve texture kept for the life of the app: the overlay pass runs only during startup (about 80 passes) and then stops. Fix in progress: one target per size, freed after 60 frames unused (GpuRenderer::next_frame, called each frame from render_tree_with_motion_opt). Measured: toy macOS 192-197 -\u003e 169-176 MB footprint (graphics 61 -\u003e 43 MB), NUC own+GPU 185 -\u003e 170 MB (GPU 115 -\u003e 99 MB). Startup reallocation gone (4 targets made). The remaining extra graphics on macOS is two 1790x1100 layer_texture entries (~16 MB).","files":null}]}